! =============================================================================
! Tutorial Problem #10 (manual): Plating Out of Noble Metals in the MSRE
! =============================================================================
! System: Mo-Pd-Ru-Rh-Tc. 434 C, 1 atm. Masses converted from the manual's
! gram values (7.7 g Mo, 5.4 g Pd, 6.6 g Ru, 0.51 g Rh, 1.3 g Tc) to moles.
! Teaching point: predict which phases noble-metal fission products form on
! a heat exchanger surface, given a known bulk composition, temperature, and
! pressure -- directly relevant to corrosion/heat-transfer analysis of plated
! deposits.
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/manual/tut10_noble_metal_plating.ti
! Verified output (matches the manual's Table 9 distribution):
!   two miscible HCPN phases (one Ru/Mo-rich, one Tc/Rh-rich), a Mo-rich BCCN
!   phase, and the stoichiometric compound Pd11Mo9_s1(s).
!   Pd: 98.7% in Pd11Mo9_s1(s), negligible elsewhere.
!   Ru: 99.2% in the Ru/Mo-rich HCPN phase.
!   Rh: 86.6% in the Tc/Rh-rich HCPN phase.
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 434
pressure          = 1.0
mass(42)          = 0.080242
mass(45)          = 0.004956
mass(43)          = 0.013265
mass(44)          = 0.065301
mass(46)          = 0.050742
temperature unit  = C
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/MoPdRuRhTc-Kaye.dat
print mode        = 2
